FontLog: "# Budapest music font+AAoACgAA-The **Budapest music font** is a music notation font digitalized from the plate engraving font used in **Editio Musica Budapest** (EMB)'s complete edition of **Liszt**, featuring dense black noteheads and relatively thin strokes.+AAoACgAA-The font is licensed under [SIL Open Font License 1.1](https://openfontlicense.org/documents/OFL.md). Any individual or enterprise can use - including commercial use - this font for free without notifying the author otherwise.+AAoACgAA----+AAoACgAA**Note**: There exists computer-made scores in EMB's complete edition of Liszt, which uses the Pertrucci music font, one of the built-in notation fonts in Finale. Budapest music font is the digital replication of EMB's plate engraving font, which differs from Pertrucci."
